<!--
  Kitchen Templates T4 — the starter template catalog.

  Source of truth: the blindspot/ReAct catalog validation run
  (scratchpad sdd-briefs/ktmpl-catalog-design.md) — only the 6 kept
  templates (score >= 7/10) are authored here. Slot widths are
  translated from the catalog doc's shorthand to the REAL products
  this database ships:

    SINK  -> base @ 30"  (SB30 Sink Base — demo catalog)
    DRWR  -> base @ 24"  (B24/DB24 — demo catalog)
    PANTRY-> tall @ 24"  (tall_pantry / demo T24)
    module-> base, nominal 0 + repeat_ok  (module-width knob fills it)
    W     -> wall @ 24"  (demo W24)
    APPL  -> appliance_type slot; nominal = catalog default width, the
             picker's appliance dropdowns override it at instantiate.

  Rules locked by the spec (2026-07-27-kitchen-templates-design.md):
    * noupdate="0" — dimension corrections must land via -u, no deploys
      of Python needed to fix a template.
    * NO corner slots and NO filler slots in the starter set — corners
      and fillers are ENGINE-derived (corner engine M2/M3), never
      templated. L-10x8 (T4a) introduces the first corner-preference
      slot after the SB-CORNER data repair.
    * The room is never grown: templates whose defaults don't fit
      simply refuse to instantiate.

  Two catalog rows ship INACTIVE (search-invisible, picker-invisible)
  as honest placeholders — the engine can't lay them out yet:
    * PEN-10X10 — needs a free-anchor peninsula run.
    * H-14X12   — needs multi-run-per-wall + connector gaps.
-->
